# The signing key, and the one file in this repository that must never be in it.
#
# The root .gitignore already has *.pfx. This is deliberately the second rule
# rather than a redundant one: the root file is long, general, and edited for
# reasons that have nothing to do with signing, and it only takes one person
# reorganising it to remove the only thing standing between a private key and a
# public repository. This rule sits beside the key it protects, is four lines
# long, and has exactly one reason to be edited.
#
# What the key is: a self-signed certificate, so nothing trusts it until a
# person chooses to. But everyone who has installed a release HAS chosen to, and
# anyone holding this PFX can sign a package that installs under that trust as an
# upgrade. build\New-SigningSecrets.ps1 is how it reaches CI, and the rotation
# note there says what replacing it costs.
devcert.pfx
